{"id": "tea:vinaya-patrika:111", "source": "src:vinaya-patrika", "location": {"ref": "pada 111 (Gita Press; verify)"}, "paraphrase": "O Keśava, what can one say? Your creation is beyond telling — a picture drawn without colour on the wall of the void by a painter without a body; it cannot be washed away, and fearing it one suffers. Some call it true, some false, some both; Tulsī says whoever gives up all three errors knows himself.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "teachers": ["tch:tulsidas"], "concepts": ["cpt:maya"], "disputes": ["dsp:world-real-or-appearance"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vinaya-patrika:172", "source": "src:vinaya-patrika", "location": {"ref": "pada 172 (verify)"}, "paraphrase": "When shall I live this way — by the grace of Rāma, content with what comes, wanting nothing from anyone, speaking kindly, bearing harsh words, seeing no one's faults, equal in pleasure and pain?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tulsidas"], "concepts": ["cpt:marks-of-the-saint"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vinaya-patrika:174", "source": "src:vinaya-patrika", "location": {"ref": "pada 174 (Gita Press; verify)"}, "paraphrase": "Whoever does not love Rāma and Vaidehī — give him up like ten million enemies, however dear: Prahlāda gave up his father, Vibhīṣaṇa his brother, Bharata his mother, Bali his guru, the Vraja women their husbands.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tulsidas"], "obstacles": ["obs:loka-lajja"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition says Tulsī sent this song in reply to Mīrābāī's letter asking whether to leave her family (legend, chronologically doubtful).", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vinaya-patrika:opening", "source": "src:vinaya-patrika", "location": {"ref": "padas 1–c. 40"}, "paraphrase": "The Vinaya Patrikā opens with hymns to Gaṇeśa, Sūrya, Śiva, Devī, Gaṅgā, Yamunā, Kāśī, Citrakūṭa, Hanumān and others, asking each for devotion to Rāma, before the petition to Rāma himself.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "teachers": ["tch:tulsidas"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Range approximate.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
